    "the_sqrt_B_contradiction_and_choice_i": {
      "argument": "Ten colleagues echoed Colleague 19's claim that feedback forces [F] ∝ sqrt([B]). But Choice I is [F] ∝ [B] * sqrt(k2*k3*k4*k5). Precursor concentration [B] is strictly first-order linear across all ten options. The author clearly modeled standard first-order mass-action kinetics."
